# Git Commit Rules

## Format

type(scope): description

- All lowercase English
- Subject line only, no body
- No trailers (Co-Authored-By, Signed-off-by, etc.)

## Types

feat, fix, refactor, chore, docs, style, test, perf, ci, build

## Scopes

root, web, ui, typescript-config

Always prefer the detailed `scope/module` format (e.g. `web/auth`, `ui/button`). Only use a bare `scope` (e.g. `web`, `ui`) when the change genuinely spans multiple modules within that scope.

Use comma-separated scopes for cross-cutting changes across multiple scopes. When listing multiple scopes, use bare scope names only: `chore(web,ui): update shared dependency`

## Examples

- `feat(web/auth): add user list pagination`
- `fix(ui/button): handle disabled state`
- `refactor(ui/lib): simplify cn utility`
- `chore(root): update dependencies`
- `feat(web): add home page layout`
